MIID_AlchemyStone: Smithing Stone
MIID_H_AlchemyStone: A common ore found throughout the\nland. Known as a cornerstone in\nsmithing materials.
MIID_Corundum: Black-Sand Steel
MIID_H_Corundum: A high-quality ore, often found in iron\nmines. Known for its low rate of carbon\nand other impurities.
MIID_PoisonStone: Venomstone
MIID_H_PoisonStone: An ore that absorbs airborne toxins and\nstores them inside. It can be dangerous\nunless mined carefully.
MIID_WindStone: Windstone
MIID_H_WindStone: A rare ore that forms in caves with\nrelentless air currents. It contains\nthe power of the wind.
MIID_ThunderStone: Thunderstone
MIID_H_ThunderStone: A rare ore that forms in areas with frequent\nlightning strikes. It contains the power\nof lightning.
MIID_SeaStar: Sea-Star Stone
MIID_H_SeaStar: A rare ore that forms in caves near the\nocean. It contains the power of the sea.
MIID_SunStone: Sunstone
MIID_H_SunStone: A rare ore that forms in areas that are\nfrequently bathed in sunlight. It contains\nthe brilliance of the sun.
MIID_MoonStone: Lunar Stone
MIID_H_MoonStone: A rare ore that forms in dark, quiet areas.\nIt contains the radiance of the moon.
MIID_BlueSnor: Blue Snoll
MIID_H_BlueSnor: A rare ore that occasionally forms in dark,\ncold places. It glows with a pale-blue light.
MIID_Cullet: Cullet
MIID_H_Cullet: A sturdy crystal shard, found in caves\nthroughout the land. Often used in\nsmithing to sharpen blades.
MIID_MagicArray: Spellshard
MIID_H_MagicArray: A mineral that has crystallized by absorbing\nmagic over millennia. It is known for its\ndistinct shape.
MIID_WootzSteel: Wootz Steel
MIID_H_WootzSteel: An iron ore with a wood-grain pattern.\nOften used in smithing to forge\nhigh-quality weapons.
MIID_Agartium: Agarthium
MIID_H_Agartium: A durable metal with a frost-like sheen.\nWith its high melting point, working it\nrequires incredible skill.
MIID_DarkMetal: Umbral Steel
MIID_H_DarkMetal: An extremely rare, mystical metal. Some\ntheorize it originally fell to this world on\nan ancient meteorite.
MIID_FlintCrystal: Phlogiston
MIID_H_FlintCrystal: A very durable mineral, only found in\nspecific places. It creates sparks when\nstruck with the right metal.
MIID_Uranite: Ouranotite
MIID_H_Uranite: A mineral named after Mount Ouranos\nwhere it was discovered. It can determine\nthe sun's position.
MIID_NemeaStalactite: Nemearite
MIID_H_NemeaStalactite: A very rare ore found only in Nemea\nCavern. Mining it is extremely dangerous.
MIID_Orichalcum: Orichalcum
MIID_H_Orichalcum: A rare mineral with a gold sparkle. It can\nstore magic within itself and is strictly\nregulated by the temples.
MIID_Adamant: Adamantine
MIID_H_Adamant: A rare mineral with a pale sparkle.\nExtremely durable and strictly regulated\nby the temples.
MIID_WarriorStone: Warrior's Soulstone
MIID_H_WarriorStone: A rare mineral, said to be the lost essence\nof a fallen warrior whose soul failed to\nreach the underworld.
MIID_NobutaMeat: Sand-Boar Meat
MIID_H_NobutaMeat: A rich, flavorful meat, known for its\nsucculence. It is widely agreed that\nfemales produce the best cuts.
MIID_BearMeat: Bear Meat
MIID_H_BearMeat: A sweet, gamy meat. Simmering it well\nbrings forth a surprisingly refined flavor.
MIID_SeaMeat: Sea-Beast Meat
MIID_H_SeaMeat: A dark meat with the potent scent of blood.\nIt is firm yet surprisingly easy to bite\nthrough.
MIID_WolfMeat: Wolf Meat
MIID_H_WolfMeat: A tough, sinewy meat that is often\nseasoned and sun-dried into jerky.
MIID_KusarikMeat: Kusarik Meat
MIID_H_KusarikMeat: A richly flavored meat with no defining\nodor. It has a slightly sour and spicy\naftertaste.
MIID_LuffMeat: Rukh Meat
MIID_H_LuffMeat: A nutrient-rich meat, known for its\nbright-red color. Many agree it pairs\nexcellently with most dishes.
MIID_YakMeat: Yarc Meat
MIID_H_YakMeat: A tender, gamy meat known for its unique\naroma. It is commonly prepared with\nfresh herbs.
MIID_LizardMeat: Flying-Lizard Meat
MIID_H_LizardMeat: A lean meat with a fresh, airy flavor.\nOvercooking it will likely drain it of\nits flavor.
MIID_GiantMeat: Giants' Meat
MIID_H_GiantMeat: A bone-in meat favored by giants. It is\nfermented, bringing forth a peculiar\nand distinctive flavor.
MIID_WoodliceMeat: Louse Meat
MIID_H_WoodliceMeat: A white, translucent meat housed in a\nthick shell. It's springy to the touch with\na hearty flavor.
MIID_ScorpionMeat: Sandbael Meat
MIID_H_ScorpionMeat: A pale, fibrous meat with a similar flavor\nto crustaceans. Surprisingly few parts of\nthis animal are edible.
MIID_SandwormMeat: Sandworm Meat
MIID_H_SandwormMeat: A firm, chewy meat with a deep flavor.\nDesert dwellers see it as a valuable\nsource of protein.
MIID_AmidGoby: Talto Goby
MIID_AmidGoby_Tut: Goby Leftovers
MIID_H_AmidGoby: A common Dagdan freshwater fish. It is\nsmall and flat with bones that can be\nremoved or eaten whole.
MIID_AmidPike: Baal Pike
MIID_H_AmidPike: A common freshwater fish of Lake Baal\nknown for its notable lifespan and size.\nIts meat is pleasantly sweet.
MIID_Megaminotsukai: Paradise Fish
MIID_H_Megaminotsukai: A legendary fish, also known as the divine\ntrout. It is said to strengthen the body\nwhen consumed.
MIID_CarneBonito: Carna Bonito
MIID_H_CarneBonito: A large, carnivorous open-sea fish. Its meat\nis thick and rich, and can be prepared in\nmany ways.
MIID_HeartBonito: Heart Bonito
MIID_H_HeartBonito: A large, carnivorous open-sea fish known\nfor the pattern on its head. It only resides\nin certain areas.
MIID_GoldTrout: Golden Trout
MIID_H_GoldTrout: A sweet fish with beautiful, golden scales.\nIt can survive in both freshwater and\nsaltwater habitats.
MIID_WhiteTrout: White Trout
MIID_H_WhiteTrout: A salty fish with silvery-white scales. It\ncan survive in both freshwater and\nsaltwater habitats.
MIID_Calednisgaa: Kothar Gar
MIID_H_Calednisgaa: A freshwater fish known for its incredibly\nthick scales. It hides in areas with relatively\nlow currents.
MIID_Yumenosilbe: Dreamtracer
MIID_H_Yumenosilbe: A rare fish with extremely high nutritional\nvalue. It prefers to live in rough seas.
MIID_LilFish: Lir Fish
MIID_H_LilFish: A fish found widely in the Lir Sea. It is\nsmall but fiercely aggressive, often tearing\nthrough fishing nets.
MIID_BazariShark: Bazari Shark
MIID_H_BazariShark: A large, ferocious fish known to hunt in\npacks. It is valuable but intelligent enough\nto avoid capture.
MIID_GalaMerlin: Garla Marlin
MIID_H_GalaMerlin: A deep-sea fish with immense strength and\na large, sharp beak. It can be incredibly\ndifficult to catch.
MIID_TortatesLoach: Ladon Loach
MIID_H_TortatesLoach: A resilient freshwater fish that can thrive\nin polluted habitats. Best purged of mud\nbefore cooking.
MIID_TortatesPike: Ladon Pike
MIID_H_TortatesPike: A freshwater fish found in large lakes.\nIt has a powerful odor and requires\nexpert preparation.
MIID_BlackRoach: Black Loach
MIID_H_BlackRoach: A very rare fish found only in certain lakes.\nIts unique taste can become addicting\nfor some.
MIID_Rahran: Rahlan
MIID_H_Rahran: A fish found in the Lir Sea. Known for its\ndistinct flavor, it can only be prepared\nproperly by expert chefs.
MIID_AngusPike: Aegis Pike
MIID_H_AngusPike: A fish with a flat body resembling a shield.\nIts dried form is considered a delicacy.
MIID_QueenRoach: Queen Loach
MIID_H_QueenRoach: A freshwater fish commonly found in lakes.\nWith its elegance, it is often called the\nQueen of the Lake.
MIID_AlbineHerring: Albinean Herring
MIID_H_AlbineHerring: A migratory fish that travels along cold\ncurrents. Its mild flavor is consistent\ndespite how it's cooked.
MIID_MeltFish: Meltfish
MIID_H_MeltFish: A deep-sea fish found in the Pasha\nCurrents. Incredibly fatty and delicious,\nbut fills the stomach quickly.
MIID_Dougzandi: Dagdandi
MIID_H_Dougzandi: An ancient freshwater-lake fish with a\nstriking appearance. Drying it brings\nforth a deep flavor.
MIID_DarkFish: Bedfish
MIID_H_DarkFish: A rare fish found in both seas and lakes.\nBecause it lives in extremely deep waters,\nit is rarely caught.
MIID_MoonFish: Moonfish
MIID_H_MoonFish: A mythical fish that only lives in certain\nlakes. Legends spin tales of its radiant\nglow on moonlit nights.
MIID_GradyGoby: Grady Goby
MIID_H_GradyGoby: A common fish found in the Lir Sea. It is\noften spotted beneath the seabed, peeking\nout curiously.
MIID_Zotogon: Zotogon
MIID_H_Zotogon: A freshwater fish often found in lakes.\nIt spoils quickly, so it is typically sold in\na processed form.
MIID_Scylla: Skolai
MIID_H_Scylla: An octopus that lives on the seabed and\nhas a sturdy shell protecting its head.\nIt is delicious when boiled.
MIID_HardFish: Steelfish
MIID_H_HardFish: A rugged fish known for its thick exterior.\nIts flesh has a light, elegant flavor.
MIID_SugarMerlin: Sugar Marlin
MIID_H_SugarMerlin: A migratory fish with a short beak. Its meat\nis thick and sweet. It pairs well with\nmany dishes.
MIID_TeffFruit: Coffee Berries
MIID_TeffFruit_Tut: Leftover Coffee Berries
MIID_H_TeffFruit: Berries widely cultivated in the south.\nThe seeds can be removed and roasted\nthen traded as coffee in various regions.
MIID_Ginji: Ginji
MIID_H_Ginji: A fruit that grows wildly on tree trunks\nthroughout Dagda. It is typically used to\nmake ghosh.
MIID_Kimbasho: Jin Ba Jiao
MIID_H_Kimbasho: A fruit that grows wildly in forests. It is\nsweet and highly nutritious. Its leaf fiber\ncan also be harvested.
MIID_Sabakukibi: Desert Millet
MIID_H_Sabakukibi: A plant that thrives in dry regions. With\nedible kernels, it has a strong flavor and\nearthy aroma.
MIID_Baku: Bakul
MIID_H_Baku: A widely used grain. It requires ample\nwater to grow, so it is farmed in areas\nwith large rivers.
MIID_Dates: Dates
MIID_H_Dates: A sweet, drought-resistant fruit that thrives\nin the desert. It preserves excellently\nwhen dried.
MIID_BlueGinji: Blue Ginji
MIID_H_BlueGinji: A rare, mutant species of ginji. This variant\nis bright blue and is used as an ingredient\nfor shosh.
MIID_Hishibana: Caltrop Flower
MIID_H_Hishibana: A plant that grows in relatively mild\nclimates. The edible part is its distinct,\nsquare-shaped flower.
MIID_Kadam: Cadam
MIID_H_Kadam: A southern plant with shelled fruit\ncontaining oil. The shells are used\nto make containers for small items.
MIID_Angelica: Angelica
MIID_H_Angelica: A rare herb cultivated for its stems and\nleaves. It has a sweet, rich flavor and\nhigh medicinal benefits.
MIID_SemPotato: Shem Yam
MIID_H_SemPotato: A plant that thrives in humid habitats.\nIts rhizomes store well and are a great\nsource of nutrients.
MIID_Soldanella: Soldanella
MIID_H_Soldanella: Primarily found in the Solidus region. It is\nonly edible if harvested before it blooms.
MIID_Hikariboshi: Lightstar
MIID_H_Hikariboshi: A rare plant that grows in specific areas.\nIt produces large fruit at the end of its vines.
MIID_Apatia: Apatta
MIID_H_Apatia: A plant that flourishes in dry areas. Due to\nits sweetness and rarity, it can be traded\nat a high price.
MIID_Sorgi: Solgi
MIID_H_Sorgi: A plant that primarily grows in deserts.\nIt stores enough water to save dehydrated\ntravelers.
MIID_PurgatoryGrass: Torment Grass
MIID_H_PurgatoryGrass: A plant with leaves so spicy they are often\ndescribed as fiery. Highly prized as a\nrare spice.
MIID_Gurumaosa: Glirmosa
MIID_H_Gurumaosa: A beautiful plant but highly poisonous.\nMust be properly prepared before human\nconsumption. Useful as an insect repellent.
MIID_RedFlicker: Redflicker
MIID_H_RedFlicker: A pungent vegetable that grows in\nmountainous areas. Its fruit is often\ndried and used in cooking.
MIID_Agave: Agave
MIID_H_Agave: A fibrous desert plant that must have its\nthorns removed before use. Known for its\nunique, spicy flavor.
MIID_SunFruit: Thry Fruit
MIID_H_SunFruit: A plant that can grow almost anywhere.\nIts fruit is often crushed and used as\naccent flavoring.
MIID_RedKimbai: Red Kimbai
MIID_H_RedKimbai: A mutant species of the kimbai with vivid\nred flowers. Its seeds are prized for their\npotent flavor.
MIID_Crestor: Crestor
MIID_H_Crestor: A rare desert plant. Its versatile leaves\ncan be used as spices or as medicinal\ningredients.
MIID_Roca: Roca
MIID_H_Roca: A vegetable found in northern areas. Known\nfor its spherical red root, it loses spiciness\nwhen heated.
MIID_Shaktou: Shaktoh
MIID_H_Shaktou: A vegetable that thrives in heat. Its\nspiciness can even cause irritation\nto the hands when harvested.
MIID_Joppa: Jyoppa
MIID_H_Joppa: A massive fruit. It is exceptionally fragrant\nwith a slightly bitter taste. It is often\npreserved in honey.
MIID_Linaria: Linaria
MIID_H_Linaria: A common plant in Dagda, known for its\nwide array of colored flowers. It is sturdy\nand resilient.
MIID_Zange: Zang
MIID_H_Zange: A bitter vegetable that thrives in low\naltitudes. It is known to soothe the mind\nwhen ingested.
MIID_Oliva: Oliva
MIID_H_Oliva: A widespread, drought-resistant plant.\nIts edible fruit is often squeezed and\nprocessed into oil.
MIID_NoaFruit: Noa Fruit
MIID_H_NoaFruit: A mutant species of the wun fruit, only\nfound north of Nowah's Cave. Its exquisite\nfragrance is legendary.
MIID_Obroma: Obroma
MIID_H_Obroma: A southern plant with sweet, sour fruit.\nPaste made from its seeds is valued\nas a luxury ingredient.
MIID_Kimbai: Kimbai
MIID_H_Kimbai: A mountain plant with gorgeous yellow\nflowers. Its seeds are often used as a spice.
MIID_TeaTree: Tea Tree
MIID_H_TeaTree: A Lambath-region plant. Its tender new\nshoots are dried and steeped to bring out\ntheir deep fragrance.
MIID_IchiFruit: Wun Fruit
MIID_H_IchiFruit: A pleasantly bitter plant that thrives in\nhigh altitudes. It is often mistaken for the\ntoxic tew fruit.
MIID_Haksan: Hakseng
MIID_H_Haksan: A leafy fruit commonly found in the east.\nIt has a refined flavor but spoils quickly,\nturning bitter.
MIID_Enriette: Enrietto
MIID_H_Enriette: A rare nut that can grow in windy hill-lands.\nIt is highly valued as a nutritional tonic.
MIID_Pongo: Pongo
MIID_H_Pongo: A distinct vegetable that grows mainly in\nthe Melias-region plains. Known for its mild,\nslightly bitter taste.
MIID_OdeMonge: Oda Monja
MIID_H_OdeMonge: A specialty in Saramis. It is bitter, but\nsatisfying, and requires many steps\nbefore it is actually edible.
MIID_Milanilla: Miranilla
MIID_H_Milanilla: A fragrant herb from Castalia. It is delicious,\nbut consuming it in excess can cause the\nbody to smell.
MIID_DhakaMonge: Dakka Monja
MIID_H_DhakaMonge: A plant found in areas like Mount Atla.\nIt must be sun-dried multiple times\nbefore it is edible.
MIID_Denebatou: Tenebato
MIID_H_Denebatou: A bean that thrives in mountainous areas.\nFermented in some regions, it is highly\nnutritious.
MIID_Cinnamos: Cinnamos
MIID_H_Cinnamos: An herb from the Pasithea region with\nsimilar fragrance to cinnamon. Typically,\nonly its leaves are used.
MIID_Paya: Paya
MIID_H_Paya: A plant cultivated in the south and a\nspecialty in Brezarant. It has a flavor\nresembling meat.
MIID_Chrysanthemum: Pyrethrum
MIID_H_Chrysanthemum: A wild herb of the Castalia region. It works\nwell as an ornament or as insect repellent.
MIID_Hingasha: Hingosh
MIID_H_Hingasha: An extremely rare plant said to help clear\nthe mind. Legend says it was once favored\nby a great sage.
MIID_YamanGiku: Yaamanthemum
MIID_H_YamanGiku: A rare flower that only blooms in a certain\narea. Famous as a specialty product of\nYaaman village.
MIID_Tobarinara: Twalinnara
MIID_H_Tobarinara: Nuts sold in Twalinn village, gathered\nby shaking a variety of tree that only\ngrows in certain places.
MIID_Lazanibarta: Lazanibata
MIID_H_Lazanibarta: A rare herb from Pasithea. It has a\nrefreshing taste and is featured\nheavily in legends of giants.
MIID_YukiTou: Yukito
MIID_H_YukiTou: A popular vegetable. While it is rarely\nfarmed, its buds are harvested for food.
MIID_CocoMinji: Cocominj
MIID_H_CocoMinji: A southern mushroom that is rarely farmed.\nIt is a known favorite of the kusarik.
MIID_Usamos: Usamos
MIID_H_Usamos: A fragrant and popular wild herb that is\nrarely farmed. Only the root stem is edible.
MIID_Hakuren: Hakuren
MIID_H_Hakuren: A small herb that is rarely farmed. Its\nsturdy leaves are often used to help\nwith sleepiness.
MIID_Yunamei: Yuna Mei
MIID_H_Yunamei: A green-blue algae that appears to be a\nlump of soil. It is translucent, highly elastic,\nand unique in flavor.
MIID_Nineyakka: Ninokka
MIID_H_Nineyakka: A popular, luxurious plant. The bark is\nboiled to produce a high-quality sweetener.
MIID_Baskatch: Baquatti
MIID_H_Baskatch: A luxury vegetable from the Ogmios region,\nfound near the sea. It is fairly new to\npublic markets.
MIID_Almamet: Almamet
MIID_H_Almamet: A spicy fruit with a sweet aroma. Grows in\nnorthwest Dagda. It is commonly used as\na lucky charm.
MIID_Melara: Melara
MIID_H_Melara: A fungus of Northern Dagda with a\nflame-like appearance. Eating too\nmuch can lead to fainting.
MIID_Solom: Solom
MIID_H_Solom: A desert plant with an odd flavor. Found\nonly in deserts far across the sea. It is\nhighly drought-resistant.
MIID_Misanga: Mizang
MIID_H_Misanga: A unique plant that only grows in deserts\nacross the sea. Known for the way it\ntumbles in the wind.
MIID_Fugue: Fyujo
MIID_H_Fugue: A vivid-blue fruit that thrives in hot, humid\nclimates. It is popular as a preserved food.
MIID_Sharmir: Zamir
MIID_H_Sharmir: A small red fruit common to central Dagda.\nThe way this fruit hangs from its vines\nis impressive.
MIID_Riganet: Liganet
MIID_H_Riganet: An unusual fruit that grows mainly in\ncentral Dagda. Its flavor is known to\ndeepen as it grows in size.
MIID_SweetLeaf: Sweet Leaves
MIID_H_SweetLeaf: A sweet herb that grows mainly in forests.\nOften used to make mixed drinks, it is\nfavored by tavern regulars.
MIID_SpiceLeaf: Pepper Leaves
MIID_H_SpiceLeaf: An herb known to add a sharp zing to\nmixed drinks. It is a favored ingredient\nof tavern patrons.
MIID_BitterLeaf: Bitter Leaves
MIID_H_BitterLeaf: An herb that adds a light, bitter zip to\nmixed drinks. It is a favored ingredient\nof tavern patrons.
MIID_WonderLeaf: Wonder Leaves
MIID_H_WonderLeaf: An herb that adds a curiously complex\nflavor to mixed drinks. Favored by\ntavern patrons.
MIID_FishingHook: Sharp Fishhook
MIID_H_FishingHook: A piercing, high-quality fishhook carved\nfrom thick seashell. Primarily enjoyed by\nfishing enthusiasts.
MIID_SeaBook: Tome from Away
MIID_H_SeaBook: An ancient book imported from a faraway\nland. Primarily enjoyed by book lovers.
MIID_ArrowFeather: Wing Fletching
MIID_H_ArrowFeather: Arrow quills forged from waterfowl feathers.\nThey improve accuracy. Primarily enjoyed\nby archers.
MIID_CookingPedia: Home-Recipe Book
MIID_H_CookingPedia: A collection of home-cooked meals from\naround the world. Primarily enjoyed by\nthose who love to cook.
MIID_BoardGame: Ebony Game Board
MIID_H_BoardGame: A common Dagdan board game crafted\nfrom high-quality wood. Primarily\nenjoyed by board-game enthusiasts.
MIID_FinestTea: Eastern Tea Leaves
MIID_H_FinestTea: Tea leaves from the land of Sai. It is a rare,\nhigh-quality, and limited product. Primarily\nenjoyed by those who love beverages.
MIID_BeautyWater: Skin Balm
MIID_H_BeautyWater: This premium lotion from Caelus is rumored\nto be used by goddesses. Primarily enjoyed\nby fashion lovers.
MIID_SewingTools: Full Sewing Kit
MIID_H_SewingTools: A complete set of sewing essentials that are\nincredibly easy to use. Primarily enjoyed by\nfashion lovers.
MIID_TrainingPillar: Training Pillar
MIID_H_TrainingPillar: A small, stone pillar found in an ancient\nruin. Primarily enjoyed by training\nenthusiasts.
MIID_FamousPoems: Poems of the Greats
MIID_H_FamousPoems: A collection of poems from across the sea,\ncapturing the art of other cultures.\nPrimarily enjoyed by book lovers.
MIID_KittenFigurine: Kitten Figurine
MIID_H_KittenFigurine: A beautiful wooden figure carved in the\nlikeness of Smyrnos's black cat.\nPrimarily enjoyed by animal lovers.
MIID_RareSeed: Rare Southern Seeds
MIID_H_RareSeed: A rare plant species said to be found \nonly in Southern Dagda. Primarily\nenjoyed by agriculture enthusiasts.
MIID_SharpChisel: Crafting Knives
MIID_H_SharpChisel: A set of easy-to-use carving knives\nfrom Da Mina. Primarily enjoyed by\ncrafting enthusiasts.
MIID_SweetsBook: Pastry Cookbook
MIID_H_SweetsBook: A cookbook filled with recipes of nutritious\nsweets that children would love. Primarily\nenjoyed by those who love sweets.
MIID_FlowerPainting: Flower Painting
MIID_H_FlowerPainting: An intricate painting of flowers. Part of\na series by a master artist. Primarily\nenjoyed by painting lovers.
MIID_LittleDagger: Sharp Dagger
MIID_H_LittleDagger: A small, versatile dagger. Useful in a variety\nof everyday situations. Primarily enjoyed by\nweapon lovers.
MIID_SweetsBox: Box of Treats
MIID_H_SweetsBox: Elegant baked goods made with sugar and\nfragrant spices. Primarily enjoyed by\nthose who love sweets.
MIID_CaseFile: School Scandal
MIID_H_CaseFile: An adventure story about a bizarre incident\nthat unfolds at a military academy.\nPrimarily enjoyed by book lovers.
MIID_BlackSilk: Eastern Black Silk
MIID_H_BlackSilk: Glossy silk thread with a pitch-black finish\nthat draws you in. Primarily enjoyed by\nfashion lovers.
MIID_PortraitYoo: Portrait of Yu Phas
MIID_H_PortraitYoo: An extremely rare painting depicting the\ngoddess Yu Phas. Primarily enjoyed by\nthose who appreciate beauty.
MIID_FishKnife: Dual Fish Knives
MIID_H_FishKnife: Two knives of varied shape, able to slice\nthrough any fish. Primarily enjoyed by \nthose who love to cook.
MIID_ArrowheadJewelry: Arrowhead Gem
MIID_H_ArrowheadJewelry: A large, beautiful gemstone shaped like\nan arrowhead. Primarily enjoyed by\nfashion lovers.
MIID_PegasusPainting: Pegasus Panorama
MIID_H_PegasusPainting: A painting depicting a majestic landscape\nand a pegasus soaring through the sky. \nPrimarily enjoyed by painting lovers.
MIID_LleatherBag: Sturdy Rucksack
MIID_H_LleatherBag: A durable leather bag that holds far more\nthan one would expect. Primarily enjoyed\nby travel enthusiasts.
MIID_AdventureTale: Tales of Adventure
MIID_H_AdventureTale: A book summarizing the exploits of a sailor\nduring his time in Southern Dagda.\nPrimarily enjoyed by book lovers.
MIID_ArtSupplies: Pack of Pastels
MIID_H_ArtSupplies: Made with delicate pigments, these art\nsupplies produce beautiful, soft colors.\nPrimarily enjoyed by crafting enthusiasts.
MIID_DanteCollection: The Works of Dante
MIID_H_DanteCollection: Volume one of the famed writer Dante's\ngreatest plays. Primarily enjoyed by\nbook lovers.
MIID_JarredVegetables: Pickled Vegetables
MIID_H_JarredVegetables: Vegetables fermented in brine for several\nmonths. Primarily enjoyed by\nvegetable lovers.
MIID_UnusualSpices: Rare Spices
MIID_H_UnusualSpices: Extremely rare spices packed in a\nluxurious presentation box. Primarily\nenjoyed by spicy-food lovers.
MIID_VihuelaTools: Vihuela-Care Tools
MIID_H_VihuelaTools: A complete set of maintenance tools to keep\ninstruments in perfect condition. Primarily\nenjoyed by musicians.
MIID_CookingTools: Outdoor Cooking Set
MIID_H_CookingTools: A complete set of cooking utensils designed\nfor outdoor use. Primarily enjoyed by those\nwho love to cook.
MIID_LoveStory: Eastern Love Story
MIID_H_LoveStory: A tragic love story between a god and\nmortal from the land of Sai. Primarily\nenjoyed by book lovers.
MIID_BlueRose: Blue-Rose Bouquet
MIID_H_BlueRose: A bouquet of beautiful roses rarely\nfound in markets. Primarily enjoyed by\nflower lovers.
MIID_HerbaPedia: Herbal Recipe Guide
MIID_H_HerbaPedia: A specialized book on medicinal cuisine\nand recipes. Primarily enjoyed by those who\nlove to cook.
MIID_TravelingHistory: History of a Master
MIID_H_TravelingHistory: Proverbs of a mysterious old man, noted by\na king during his travels. Primarily enjoyed\nby book lovers.
MIID_TrainingWeight: Training Weights
MIID_H_TrainingWeight: Bracelets and ankle bands filled with lead\nand used in training. Primarily enjoyed\nby training enthusiasts.
MIID_SaltedFish: Brined Fish Guts
MIID_H_SaltedFish: A savory, preserved food made of fermented\nfish innards, yeast, and salt. Primarily\nenjoyed by fish lovers.
MIID_MagicTools: Magic-Trick Set
MIID_H_MagicTools: A collection of items children often use to\nperform simple magic tricks. Primarily\nenjoyed by those who appreciate spirituality.
MIID_HairOrnament: Red Hair Clip
MIID_H_HairOrnament: A vibrantly colored hair clip made of sap\nfrom a tree in the east. Primarily enjoyed\nby fashion lovers.
MIID_SalamisSweets: Saraminian Sweets
MIID_H_SalamisSweets: Simple baked goods from Saramis.\nPrimarily enjoyed by those who love sweets.
MIID_RockSugar: Candy Crystals
MIID_H_RockSugar: High-quality candy made from crystallizing\ndesert millet into sugar. Primarily enjoyed\nby those who love sweets.
MIID_RuggedWork: Rugged Blade
MIID_H_RuggedWork: An antique sword, admired by even the god\nof war. Primarily enjoyed by weapon lovers.
MIID_MorphisAlmanac: Morfis Almanac
MIID_H_MorphisAlmanac: A book detailing various events held in\nthe City of Illusion, Morfis. Primarily\nenjoyed by book lovers.
MIID_DesertThings: Desert Curios
MIID_H_DesertThings: Items from the desert, unknown in material\nand purpose.
MIID_DishesCollection: Village Recipes
MIID_H_DishesCollection: A cookbook of recipes from eastern Dagda.\nPrimarily enjoyed by those who love\nto cook.
MIID_SandwormsMeat: Meaty Delicacy
MIID_H_SandwormsMeat: Fermented sandworm innards wrapped\nin beast meat. Primarily enjoyed by\nmeat lovers.
MIID_MedicineDrops: Special "Medicine"
MIID_H_MedicineDrops: It's said that a single cup of ghosh can cure\nany mild illness. Primarily enjoyed by\nlovers of fermented drinks.
MIID_ManeOrnament: Mane Ornament
MIID_H_ManeOrnament: An ornate accessory for a horse's mane,\ncrafted from colorful yarn. Primarily\nenjoyed by those who love horses.
MIID_TrainingBracelet: Training Bracelet
MIID_H_TrainingBracelet: A hefty but beautiful training accessory.\nPrimarily enjoyed by training enthusiasts.
MIID_MealCoupon: Meal Voucher
MIID_H_MealCoupon: A coupon allowing one to eat for free at\ncertain restaurants. Primarily enjoyed by\nthose who appreciate cuisine.
MIID_FemaleKnight: The Knight's Suitors
MIID_H_FemaleKnight: The story of a female knight who challenged\nfive suitors to complete trials. Primarily\nenjoyed by book lovers.
MIID_ShieldsPortrait: Shield Portrait
MIID_H_ShieldsPortrait: A painting of the War of Grania, origin of\nSaramis's reputation as the Shield of Dagda.\nPrimarily enjoyed by painting lovers.
MIID_PottedVegetables: Potted Vegetables
MIID_H_PottedVegetables: Potted vegetables that can be harvested\nthroughout the year. Primarily enjoyed\nby vegetable lovers.
MIID_StrategyManuscrip: Strategy Manuscript
MIID_H_StrategyManuscrip: "The Great August's Art of War," a must-\nread for tacticians. Primarily enjoyed by\ntraining enthusiasts.
MIID_JointProtection: Joint-Relief Gloves
MIID_H_JointProtection: Luxurious leather gloves that protect the\narm when firing a bow. Primarily\nenjoyed by archers.
MIID_SpiritDoll: Protection Figurine
MIID_H_SpiritDoll: A doll from Brigid. It is said that spirits\nprotect the owner. Primarily enjoyed by\nthose who appreciate spirituality.
MIID_HorseCare: Horse-Grooming Kit
MIID_H_HorseCare: A collection of horse-care tools. Primarily\nenjoyed by those who love horses.
MIID_EastGame: Eastern Board Game
MIID_H_EastGame: A beautiful display piece brought from\nthe far east. Primarily enjoyed by\nboard-game enthusiasts.
MIID_DecorativeArrow: Decorative Arrows
MIID_H_DecorativeArrow: A set of three decorative arrows beautiful\nenough to even impress nobility.\nPrimarily enjoyed by archers.
MIID_FlashyBangle: Gaudy Bangle
MIID_H_FlashyBangle: A sparkling bracelet inlaid with gemstones\nand decorative carvings. Primarily enjoyed\nby fashion lovers.
MIID_StrangeVegetables: Odd Vegetable Seeds
MIID_H_StrangeVegetables: Vegetable seeds with an outer shell that\nresembles a face. Primarily enjoyed by\nagriculture enthusiasts.
MIID_CrimsonStatue: Crimson Bull Figure
MIID_H_CrimsonStatue: This statue honors Nathan the Red, also\nknown as Catoblepas. Primarily enjoyed by\nart lovers.
MIID_JadeStatue: Jade Panther Figure
MIID_H_JadeStatue: This statue honors Creek the Green, also\nknown as Pantere. Primarily enjoyed by\nart lovers.
MIID_TradeIntroduction: Trader's Handbook
MIID_H_TradeIntroduction: A book on good business practices, from\nnegotiation to cautionary tales. Primarily\nenjoyed by book lovers.
MIID_CeremonialSpear: Ceremonial Spear
MIID_H_CeremonialSpear: A beautifully decorated spear. It is not\ndurable enough for practical use.\nPrimarily enjoyed by weapon lovers.
MIID_SpiritGame: Spirit Board Game
MIID_H_SpiritGame: Board game from Brigid with spirit-themed\npieces. Primarily enjoyed by board-game\nenthusiasts.
MIID_GamesCollection: Board-Game Tactics
MIID_H_GamesCollection: A book of techniques for various board\ngames, devised by masters. Primarily\nenjoyed by board-game enthusiasts.
MIID_BeautifulRing: Exquisite Ring
MIID_H_BeautifulRing: A beautiful ring with a large gemstone and \nstrikingly decorated pieces. Primarily\nenjoyed by fashion lovers.
MIID_DougzaGrass: Dagda Beard Grass
MIID_H_DougzaGrass: An herb with an odd fragrance known to\nsoothe horses. Primarily enjoyed by\nthose who love horses.
MIID_FishingRod: Flexible Fishing Rod
MIID_H_FishingRod: A strong, flexible iron fishing rod that\nis sure to catch even the biggest fish.\nPrimarily enjoyed by fishing enthusiasts.
MIID_RoseBouquet: Red-Rose Bouquet
MIID_H_RoseBouquet: A bouquet of large, blazingly red roses.\nPrimarily enjoyed by flower lovers.
MIID_RuinsThings: Ruin Relics
MIID_H_RuinsThings: A collection of strange relics found near the\nGreat Tartarus Ruins.
MIID_FishEyeball: Huge Fish Eyeball
MIID_H_FishEyeball: The salted eye of a giant southern fish\ncaught in the port of Alecto. Primarily\nenjoyed by fish lovers.
MIID_EasternEarring: Eastern Earrings
MIID_H_EasternEarring: Beautiful gold earrings from the east with\ndeep-green beads. Primarily enjoyed by\nfashion lovers.
MIID_BaguaTools: Divination Bagua
MIID_H_BaguaTools: A tool from Sai that uses the Bagua\nsystem to tell fortunes. Primarily\nenjoyed by fortune tellers.
MIID_ThickBook: Thick Foreign Tome
MIID_H_ThickBook: A book from Fódlan about spirit magic.\nPrimarily enjoyed by book lovers.
MIID_ArenaStory: Tales of the Arena
MIID_H_ArenaStory: A collection of stories about the exploits of\nvarious gladiators. Primarily enjoyed by\nbook lovers.
MIID_BowTools: Bow Repair Kit
MIID_H_BowTools: A collection of tools that help one maintain\ntheir bow. Primarily enjoyed by archers.
MIID_PickledBulbs: Pickled Bulbs
MIID_H_PickledBulbs: A sour, preserved food made by pickling\nvegetable bulbs in vinegar. Primarily\nenjoyed by vegetable lovers.
MIID_FlavorfulSeasoning: Strong Seasonings
MIID_H_FlavorfulSeasoning: A condiment with a strong umami flavor.\nMade by mixing spices and seafood.\nPrimarily enjoyed by those who love to cook.
MIID_SmallTeff: Common Coffee
MIID_H_SmallTeff: An unremarkable coffee made from roasted,\nlow-quality beans. Primarily enjoyed by\nthose who love coffee.
MIID_LargeTeff: Select Coffee
MIID_H_LargeTeff: Coffee made from large, carefully selected\nbeans. Primarily enjoyed by those who\nlove coffee.
MIID_SouthTeff: Southern Coffee
MIID_H_SouthTeff: A fragrant, high-quality coffee made from\nsouthern beans. Primarily enjoyed by those\nwho love coffee.
MIID_AugusTeff: Orgus Coffee
MIID_H_AugusTeff: A rare, strong coffee from Mount Orgus.\nPrimarily enjoyed by those who love coffee.
MIID_SolomonTeff: Solomon Coffee
MIID_H_SolomonTeff: The legendary coffee of Solomon, unique in\naroma and flavor. Primarily enjoyed by\nthose who love coffee.
MIID_YoungGauche: Young Ghosh
MIID_H_YoungGauche: A recently brewed ghosh with a sharp,\nfruity flavor. Primarily enjoyed by lovers\nof fermented drinks.
MIID_AgingGauche: Mature Ghosh
MIID_H_AgingGauche: A well-aged ghosh with a deep aroma and\nflavor. Primarily enjoyed by lovers of\nfermented drinks.
MIID_GreenGauche: Jade Ghosh
MIID_H_GreenGauche: A rare jade-colored ghosh only produced\nin certain regions. Primarily enjoyed by\nlovers of fermented drinks.
MIID_SunGauche: Sun Ghosh
MIID_H_SunGauche: Ghosh with a strong, bright flavor. It is often\nproduced in dry regions. Primarily enjoyed\nby lovers of fermented drinks.
MIID_SecretGauche: Secret Ghosh
MIID_H_SecretGauche: Ghosh made from a recipe so delicious that\nit is kept secret. Primarily enjoyed by lovers\nof fermented drinks.
MIID_VolcanoGauche: Volcano Ghosh
MIID_H_VolcanoGauche: Brewed near a volcano, this is a common\nceremonial ghosh. Primarily enjoyed by\nlovers of fermented drinks.
MIID_CrimsonGauche: Crimson Ghosh
MIID_H_CrimsonGauche: A stunningly red ghosh known as a votive\noffering to temples. Primarily enjoyed by\nlovers of fermented drinks.
MIID_SouthGauche: Southern Ghosh
MIID_H_SouthGauche: Imported ghosh from Mosa with a very\nbold, rich flavor. Primarily enjoyed by \nlovers of fermented drinks.
MIID_ExcitingGauche: Energizing Ghosh
MIID_H_ExcitingGauche: Ghosh from Saramis with a strong, spicy\nflavor. Primarily enjoyed by lovers of\nfermented drinks.
MIID_RusticGauche: Rustic Ghosh
MIID_H_RusticGauche: Special ghosh from a small village, rarely\nsold in markets. Primarily enjoyed by\nlovers of fermented drinks.
MIID_YoungSoush: Young Shosh
MIID_H_YoungSoush: A recently brewed shosh known for its\ndistinct blue color. Primarily enjoyed by\nlovers of fermented drinks.
MIID_AgingSoush: Mature Shosh
MIID_H_AgingSoush: A well-aged shosh with a deep, mellow\nflavor. Primarily enjoyed by lovers of\nfermented drinks.
MIID_MellowSoush: Aromatic Shosh
MIID_H_MellowSoush: A rare shosh with a rich flavor, brewed with\na secret technique. Primarily enjoyed by\nlovers of fermented drinks.
MIID_WittySoush: Light Shosh
MIID_H_WittySoush: A light-textured shosh only made in a\ncertain village. Primarily enjoyed by\nlovers of fermented drinks.
MIID_BlueSoush: Blue Shosh
MIID_H_BlueSoush: A refreshing, light shosh known for its\nunique, sky-blue color. Primarily enjoyed\nby lovers of fermented drinks.
MIID_ThinServi: Weak Cervi
MIID_H_ThinServi: Cervi commonly diluted with water.\nPrimarily enjoyed by children.
MIID_AgingServi: Strong Cervi
MIID_H_AgingServi: Fresh, rich cervi. Its sweetness and acidity\nmake it difficult to drink. Primarily enjoyed\nby children.
MIID_DryingServi: Mature Dried Cervi
MIID_H_DryingServi: Dried sediment from cervi. A light,\nnutritious preserve. Primarily enjoyed\nby children.
MIID_GinjiServi: Ginji Cervi
MIID_H_GinjiServi: A fruity cervi, made with a mountain of\nginji fruit mixed in. Primarily enjoyed\nby those who love sweets.
MIID_WhiteServi: Pure-White Cervi
MIID_H_WhiteServi: A refreshing cervi with very few impurities.\nPrimarily enjoyed by those who love sweets.
MIID_Garm: Garum
MIID_H_Garm: A salty, umami-flavored fish sauce typically\nmade in waterside towns. Primarily enjoyed\nby those who love to cook.
MIID_LightGarm: Smooth Garum
MIID_H_LightGarm: A garum strained multiple times, creating a\nnoticeably clean flavor. Primarily enjoyed by\nthose who love to cook.
MIID_RichGarm: Concentrated Garum
MIID_H_RichGarm: Garum that has been boiled down into its\npurest, richest form. Primarily enjoyed by\nthose who love to cook.
MIID_AlectoGarm: Alecto Garum
MIID_H_AlectoGarm: A luxurious garum from Alecto with a\ndistinct, rich flavor. Primarily enjoyed\nby those who love to cook.
MIID_NizaGarm: Niiza Garum
MIID_H_NizaGarm: Garum from Niiza Port. Commonly used in\ntrade with Fódlan. Primarily enjoyed by\nthose who love to cook.
MIID_LegendaryGarm: Legendary Garum
MIID_H_LegendaryGarm: An extremely rare garum aged within a\nsunken ship. Primarily enjoyed by those\nwho love to cook.
MIID_NastyGarm: Rancid Garum
MIID_H_NastyGarm: A terrible-smelling garum specially crafted\nby a certain nobleman. Primarily enjoyed\nby those who love to cook.
MIID_MorphisTea: Morfis Tea
MIID_H_MorphisTea: Black tea from Morfis, aged to a deeper\nflavor through a special process. Primarily\nenjoyed by those who love beverages.
MIID_FodlanTea: Fódlan Tea
MIID_H_FodlanTea: Black tea imported from Fódlan and scented\nwith rose petals. Primarily enjoyed by those\nwho love beverages.
MIID_JermellMilk: Jamel Milk
MIID_H_JermellMilk: Milk from a jamel. It has a distinct aroma\nand subtle salty taste. Primarily enjoyed\nby children.
MIID_YakMilk: Yarc Milk
MIID_H_YakMilk: Milk from a yarc. It is known for its\nnutritional benefits. Primarily enjoyed\nby children.
MIID_HoneyMilk: Honey Milk
MIID_H_HoneyMilk: The perfect blend of yarc milk and honey,\nmaking it that much more enticing.\nPrimarily enjoyed by those who love sweets.
MIID_RusticTreats: Simple Pastries
MIID_H_RusticTreats: A collection of baked goods that are easy\nto enjoy and never get old. Primarily\nenjoyed by those who love sweets.
MIID_SweetTreats: Mellow Pastries
MIID_H_SweetTreats: Baked treats with a slightly sweet taste,\nmade with juice from desert millet.\nPrimarily enjoyed by those who love sweets.
MIID_FragrantTreats: Fragrant Pastries
MIID_H_FragrantTreats: Fragrant sweets often baked in a\nhigh-temperature oven. Primarily\nenjoyed by those who love sweets.
MIID_HoneyTreats: Honey Pastries
MIID_H_HoneyTreats: Baked sweets made with a sizable amount\nof honey. Primarily enjoyed by those who\nlove sweets.
MIID_TeffTreats: Coffee Pastries
MIID_H_TeffTreats: Sweet and sour baked goods made with\ncoffee beans. Primarily enjoyed by those\nwho love sweets.
MIID_AntiqueMedal: Antique Medal
MIID_H_AntiqueMedal: A military medal awarded to those who\nearn renown in battle. Primarily enjoyed\nby those who revere martial achievements.
MIID_ImitationEmblem: Imitation Medal
MIID_H_ImitationEmblem: A cheap replica of a military medal from\nancient times. Primarily enjoyed by those\nwho revere martial achievements.
MIID_BlackFeather: Black Tail Feathers
MIID_H_BlackFeather: Black ornius feathers known for being\nhigh-quality decorative items. Primarily\nenjoyed by fashion lovers.
MIID_CommonPeople: Everyday Scenes
MIID_H_CommonPeople: A slapstick comedy about the everyday lives\nof ordinary people. Primarily enjoyed by\nbook lovers.
MIID_DyedTowel: Ahm Lu Cloth
MIID_H_DyedTowel: Stitched in Ahm Lu and patterned after\na flower beloved by Yu Phas. Primarily\nenjoyed by those who appreciate beauty.
MIID_MegrezSand: Megrez Soil
MIID_H_MegrezSand: Soil from the Ruins of Megrez.\nIt doesn't seem out of the ordinary.\nDeliver it right away.
MIID_AeginaCrystal: Aegina Crystal
MIID_H_AeginaCrystal: A colored crystal that represents mercy,\nharmony, and perfection. Get this delivered\nright away.
MIID_OldPendant: Spellcaster's Relics
MIID_H_OldPendant: A box of stolen goods. Just holding it makes\none feel like they're being watched. You\nshould deliver it soon.
MIID_ZealCoins: Djilu Coin
MIID_H_ZealCoins: A rare coin from a southern nation that was\ndestroyed ages ago. You should get this to\nthe client quickly.
MIID_JuraWoodcarving: Jurah Carving
MIID_H_JuraWoodcarving: A wooden carving of a goddess, made by a\nskilled craftsman. Deliver it right away.
MIID_RedSecretLetter: Sealed Letter
MIID_H_RedSecretLetter: A private letter meant only for the\nrecipient. Deliver it when you can.
MIID_Blushing: Mature Blush
MIID_H_Blushing: Makeup perfect for capturing that unique,\nmature look. Get this over to Esmeralda.
MIID_JuraStatue: Statue of Jurah
MIID_H_JuraStatue: A statue of the goddess Jurah. Just looking\nat it brings peace and calm. Deliver it when\nyou can.
MIID_CarlaStatue: Statue of Kalla
MIID_H_CarlaStatue: A statue of the goddess Kalla. Even as a\nstatue, it exudes beauty. You should\ndeliver it right away.
MIID_YufasStatue: Statue of Yu Phas
MIID_H_YufasStatue: A statue of the goddess Yu Phas. It has a\nkind, tender aura. You should deliver it to\nthe client right away.
MIID_PhotonStatue: Statue of Fortuna
MIID_H_PhotonStatue: A statue of the goddess Fortuna. It almost\nseems sad somehow. Deliver it to the\nclient soon.
MIID_Harness: Custom Axle
MIID_H_Harness: A custom axle for carriages, made by\nmaster craftsmen in Megaira. Deliver it\nwhen you can.
MIID_MansionKey: Winged-Lion Key
MIID_H_MansionKey: An antique key with a winged lion carved\ninto it. Seems to be the key to a home.\nDeliver it when you can.
MIID_GiscoTreasure: Gisco's Treasure
MIID_H_GiscoTreasure: A jewelry box with a mermaid on it, left\nbehind by the Flame Lord Gisco. Deliver\nit when you can.
MIID_VioletBrooch: Violet Brooch
MIID_H_VioletBrooch: A delicate brooch belonging to Creek's\nsister. Deliver it to him when you can.
MIID_SandbaalTail: Sandbael Tails
MIID_H_SandbaalTail: A bundle of desert scorpion tails. You\nshould get this to the client as soon\nas you can.
MIID_GirlClip: Girl's Hair Clip
MIID_H_GirlClip: A small hair clip dropped by someone\nwhile she was merely playing. You should\nreturn it.
MIID_SpecialGinji: Rare Ginji
MIID_H_SpecialGinji: A rare, multi-colored ginji fruit known for\nits unique appearance and flavor. Get this\ndelivered soon.
MIID_GiftBox: Mother's Gift
MIID_H_GiftBox: An item Ultand's mother prepared for her\nfamily. Return it to Ultand right away.
MIID_PoetsMonument: Monument Verse
MIID_H_PoetsMonument: A verse from the monument of a legendary\npoet. Return it to Sirocco right away.
MIID_GlowDrop: Scarlet Firedrops
MIID_H_GlowDrop: Rare black tea from Creusa, known for its\ncolor and fragrance. Get this over to\nOlympia right away.
MIID_DesertRose: Aurum Rose
MIID_H_DesertRose: A rare, golden rose that sprouts in strong\nsunlight. You should gift it to Olympia\nright away.
MIID_BlueHeart: Azure Heart
MIID_H_BlueHeart: A crystal with a captivating blue sparkle.\nOffer it to Olympia.
MIID_GoldHelmet: Golden Helm
MIID_H_GoldHelmet: Beautiful and ornate golden armor owned\nby Mars. Return it to Mars as soon\nas you can.
MIID_DesertSunStone: Desert Sunstone
MIID_H_DesertSunStone: A stone that has been absorbing the power\nof the sun for a long time. Return it to\nCredna soon.
MIID_Sandalwood: Sandalwood
MIID_H_Sandalwood: Wood with a fragrant scent that has long\nbeen used as a charm against evil. Get this\nto Kalla soon.
MIID_DagdaShield: Dagda's Godshield
MIID_H_DagdaShield: A protective covering that was once part\nof Emperor Dagda but was lost in battle.\nDeliver it to Jurah.
MIID_Fulama: Flamma
MIID_H_Fulama: A vial of suspicious liquid rumored to grant\nsupernatural powers. Deliver this while\nyou can.
MIID_AncientStone: Ancient Tablet
MIID_H_AncientStone: A stone slab etched with strange symbols.\nIt's old but in good condition. Deliver it\nwhen you can.
MIID_AmalfridaSword: Treasured Sword
MIID_H_AmalfridaSword: A sword forged for Elana of Arago, also\nknown as the "Lady of Dawn." Get this\ndelivered right away.
MIID_SoulCrystal: Soul Crystal
MIID_H_SoulCrystal: A rare gem, said to be the crystallized\nessence of a soul. Deliver this as soon\nas you can.
MIID_JuniorLicense: Beginner License
MIID_H_JuniorLicense: A temple-issued license, required to take\nthe certification exam for beginner classes.
MIID_InterLicense: Specialty License
MIID_H_InterLicense: A temple-issued license, required to take\nthe certification exam for mid-level,\nspecialty classes.
MIID_HighLicense: Advanced License
MIID_H_HighLicense: A temple-issued license, required to take\nthe certification exam for high-level,\nadvanced classes.
MIID_HighestLicense: Master License
MIID_H_HighestLicense: A temple-issued license, required to take\nthe certification exam for master classes,\nthe highest level of achievement.
MIID_TankLicense: Charioteer License
MIID_H_TankLicense: A temple-issued license, required to become\na charioteer, a class focused on breaking\nthrough foes.
MIID_ElephantLicense: Elephant License
MIID_H_ElephantLicense: A temple-issued license, required to become\nan elephant rider who rides a war elephant\ninto battle.
MIID_ReincarnationLotus: Lotus of Reincarnation
MIID_H_ReincarnationLotus: A rare item bestowed by the gods. Allows\nthe owner to take the test of the avatar.
MIID_MusaNecklace: Muses' Necklace
MIID_H_MusaNecklace: A rare item bestowed by the gods. Allows\nthe owner to take the test of the apsara.
MIID_EmperorBand: Emperor's Sash
MIID_H_EmperorBand: A rare item bestowed by the gods. Allows\nthe owner to take the test of the godhand.
MIID_TridentSpear: Trident
MIID_H_TridentSpear: A rare item bestowed by the gods. Allows\nthe owner to take the test of the trident.
MIID_DarknessCrystal: Crystal of Darkness
MIID_H_DarknessCrystal: A rare item bestowed by the gods. Allows\nthe owner to take the test of the calamity.
MIID_DemonTsuba: Demonic Swordguard
MIID_H_DemonTsuba: A rare item bestowed by the gods. Allows\nthe owner to take the test of the blade.
MIID_IronSaddle: Divinium Saddle
MIID_H_IronSaddle: A rare item bestowed by the gods. Allows\nthe owner to take the test of the cavalier.
MIID_JudgmentBalance: Scales of Judgment
MIID_H_JudgmentBalance: A rare item bestowed by the gods. Allows\nthe owner to take the test of the eternal.
MIID_Materials: Building Materials
MIID_H_Materials: Materials for Dagsion's restoration. With\nthese, the great city can finally rise again.
MIID_CrownKey: Key of the Diadem
MIID_H_CrownKey: A key to the temple of the Diadem, said\nto hold grace promised by the progenitor\ngod, Sothis.
MIID_DancerLicense: Dancer's Necklace
MIID_H_DancerLicense: Grants training in a class that focuses on\ndance. An heirloom passed down through\nthe generations. 
MIID_SpecialCargo: Company Cargo
MIID_H_SpecialCargo: Vandahl Trading Company cargo that went\nmissing during transport. You must retrieve\nit all.
